Installation
============

Possible extras:

{% if include_cli %}- ``cli``: Installs typer and adds ``{{github_repo_name}}`` as a command.
{% endif %}{% if include_tui %}- ``tui``: Installs textual and adds ``{{github_repo_name}}-tui`` as a command.
{% endif %}{% if include_web %}- ``web``: Installs {% if web_framework == "litestar" %}Litestar{% else %}FastAPI{% endif %} and adds ``{{github_repo_name}}-web`` as a command.
{% endif %}{% if include_mcp %}- ``mcp``: Installs the MCP SDK and adds ``{{github_repo_name}}-mcp`` as a command.
{% endif %}{% if include_worker %}- ``worker``: Installs FastStream and adds ``{{github_repo_name}}-worker`` as a command.
{% endif %}{% if include_pydantic_settings %}- ``config``: Installs pydantic-settings.
{% endif %}- ``all``: Installs all extras if available.

Stable release
--------------

{% if include_cli or include_tui or include_gui or include_web or include_mcp or include_worker -%}
{% set app_command = github_repo_name if include_cli else (github_repo_name ~ "-tui" if include_tui else (github_repo_name ~ "-gui" if include_gui else (github_repo_name ~ "-web" if include_web else (github_repo_name ~ "-mcp" if include_mcp else github_repo_name ~ "-worker")))) -%}
``{{github_repo_name}}`` is an end-user application, so install it into an
isolated environment with your preferred tool installer (the ``all`` extra pulls
in the runtime dependencies that live behind the component extras):

.. code-block:: sh

   uv tool install '{{github_repo_name}}[all]'

.. code-block:: sh

   pipx install '{{github_repo_name}}[all]'

Or run it once without installing:

.. code-block:: sh

   {% if include_cli %}uvx '{{github_repo_name}}[all]'{% else %}uvx --from '{{github_repo_name}}[all]' {{app_command}}{% endif %}

To add ``{{github_repo_name}}`` as a dependency of another project instead, use
``uv add '{{github_repo_name}}[all]'`` or ``pip install '{{github_repo_name}}[all]'``.
{% else -%}
To install ``{{github_repo_name}}``, run this command in your terminal:

.. code-block:: sh

   uv add {{github_repo_name}}

Or if you prefer to use ``pip``:

.. code-block:: sh

   pip install {{github_repo_name}}
{% endif %}
From source
-----------

The source files for ``{{github_repo_name}}`` can be downloaded from the
`GitHub repo <https://github.com/{{github_user}}/{{github_repo_name}}>`_.

You can either clone the public repository:

.. code-block:: sh

   git clone https://github.com/{{github_user}}/{{github_repo_name}}.git

Or download the
`tarball <https://github.com/{{github_user}}/{{github_repo_name}}/tarball/main>`_:

.. code-block:: sh

   mkdir {{github_repo_name}}
   curl -fL https://github.com/{{github_user}}/{{github_repo_name}}/tarball/main | tar -xz --strip-components=1 -C {{github_repo_name}}

Once you have a copy of the source, you can install it with:

.. code-block:: sh

   cd {{github_repo_name}}
   uv pip install .
